@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: CREATE A REPORT</b>
  --
  New definition | Party ACMCOR | Tenant administrator
  --
  <b>1. IDENTITY</b>
  --
  {#
    Field | Value
    Name | Intraday Exposure
    Description | Exposure profiles, trading book
    Report type | risk
    Is official | yes
    Party | ACMCOR, from the session
  }
  --
  <b>2. WHAT THE TYPE NEEDS</b>
  --
  {#
    Configuration type | Required by risk
    conventions | required
    pricing_engines | required
    todays_market | required
    curve_configuration | required
    risk_report_config | required
  }
  The list is report_type_configuration_types.list, read for risk. Nothing
  answers a requirement beyond it.
  --
  <b>3. THE CONFIGURATIONS THE DEFINITION BINDS</b>
  --
  {#
    Slot | Configuration
    conventions | Group conventions
    pricing_engines | Group pricing engines
    todays_market | Group today's market
    curve_configuration | Group curve configuration
    risk_report_config | Exposure simulation
  }
  {
    [ Bind a configuration ]
  }
  What each slot supplies, in the words the screen uses: conventions, the
  instrument conventions the trades are read with; pricing engines, the pricing
  model of each product and its parameters; today's market, the market data a run
  prices against by market role; curve configuration, the curves, their
  bootstrapping, segments, volatilities and correlations; risk report config, the
  run settings a party shares, the base currency, the observation model, the VaR
  and SIMM settings and threading, and the scope.
  --
  <b>4. THE ANALYTICS AND THEIR SETTINGS</b>
  --
  {#
    On | Analytic | Order | Settings
    Y | npv | 1 | baseCurrency GBP
    Y | simulation | 2 | baseCurrency GBP
    Y | pfe | 3 | quantile 0.95
    N | saccr | 4 | -
    N | sensitivity | 5 | -
  }
  Fourteen analytic types are offered. Each carries an active toggle, a display
  order, and its own parameter rows.
  {
    [ Add an analytic ] | [ Edit its parameters ]
  }
  An analytic is turned off by setting active false. Nothing is deleted.
  --
  <b>REFUSED: pfe WITHOUT simulation</b>
  --
  pfe reads the cube that simulation writes, so a definition that enables pfe
  without simulation cannot work. The rule lives in the ACME seeder,
  check_exposure_needs_simulation, and not in the reporting service. Nothing
  validates it when a definition is written.
  --
  <b>5. SCOPE</b>
  --
  {#
    Portfolio | Scoped by
    Group Treasury Portfolio | not scoped
    Trading Book | Exposure simulation
  }
  The bound configuration is named Exposure simulation - Trading Book after the
  analytics set and the scope it carries. The scope is a column of that
  configuration and not a field of the definition, and no operation here writes
  it: a portfolio no bound configuration is scoped to cannot be chosen.
  --
  <b>6. REVIEW: WHAT WILL BE WRITTEN</b>
  --
  {#
    Written | Operation
    definition | report_definitions.put
    five binds | report_configurations.put
    analytics | configuration_analytics.put_many
    parameters | configuration_analytic_parameters.put
  }
  name Intraday Exposure, report_type risk, is_official true, schedule_expression
  none, scheduler_job_id none, concurrency_policy skip, pre_processing execute,
  prepared_input_key null, post_processing execute; npv, simulation and pfe
  active true at orders 1, 2 and 3; baseCurrency GBP and quantile 0.95.
  The definition is on demand.
  {
    [ Save the report ] | [ Back ]
  }
  --
  <b>7. AFTER THE WRITE: READ BACK</b>
  --
  {#
    Field | Read back
    id | a new identifier
    version | 1
    schedule_expression | -
    scheduler_job_id | -
    runs | never run
  }
  The definition is bitemporal, so an edit writes a new version and no past run
  changes. The front door draws this definition as never run.
  {
    [ Leave it on demand ] | [ Choose when it runs ]
  }
  --
  <b>WHAT THIS SCREEN CANNOT SHOW</b>
  --
  No operation answers what a report needs in order to run beyond the
  configuration types its report type requires. Nothing validates the
  pfe-needs-simulation rule on write. No operation writes the portfolio scope.
  No BFF route serves reporting, and nothing in the application creates a report
  today.
}

@enduml
